 and by the way  tomorrow I get on a plane and hit the  road running and  we're gonna go lock up that next film  for everybody so you you've also you had  a great panel already are you doing  something here at the booth this weekend  as well yeah yeah so part of the Marvel  master works collection I'm doing an  unboxing the packaging that this stuff  comes in is truly amazing I created a  Stark Industries experience so it comes  in a Stark Industries case you open it  up there's lots of fun little secret  cool things that I'm about to unveil  downstairs that come with this product  and literally my goal was to make every  bit of this experience collectible  you're not going to want to throw away  the cardboard box it comes in so it's  pretty cool and and you know it's out of  my wheelhouse but I embraced it for  Disney Marvel Kevin Feige and the true  honest collector so check it out I do  want to get to a fan question because we  have a bunch sitting here yeah um  someone would like to know if you've  kept any props for yourself and if so  win and will you get in trouble no no  there's some props that you know that  lie around in my shop but under contract  Marvel owns everything just so you know  but but but because I've been with them  for so long I have access to all the  props like we have a huge warehouse we  have a hundred and forty cap shield  sitting around because the life  expectancy of a cap shield is only three  scenes before it's damaged beyond repair  and then we make more so so we have  access to all this stuff but I don't  really like in the first five years of  my my career which was over 30 years ago  I would keep some props and I'd hang  them up on the wall but things kind of  got cluttered after 30  two years a lot of props went through my  my house and so now I just have a proper  house where I don't keep any props but I  have a huge warehouse full of everything  so it's kind of cool and if I'm allowed  one more what has been the hardest  problem for you to find or assemble I am  to say that I don't want to use the word  hard but the most challenging prob was  probably the arc reactor originally in  figuring that out so we thought we'd  open to a bunch of research about  nuclear power and cold fusion and how do  we create an electromagnet that will  keep trap kn'l from your heart because  we know that the shrapnel was barbed  from the Stark Industries bomb and every  breath you take the shrapnel goes closer  and closer to your heart and we had to  create something that would do that now  the big challenge was it's supposed to  look like it's four inches into his  chest right and so I used a lot of force  perspective work so I started with a big  ring and go to a smaller and smaller and  smaller and smaller ring which to the  eye gives you the illusion that it's  deeper and deeper  I think that's an old trick like from  the Alfred Hitchcock days where they  would have long hallways that come down  to nothing so that it would look longer  and they were shooting onstage so I sort  of look at all that I looked at like  film your sort of attitude mixed with a  hi-tech attitude and we came up with the  arc reactor and it's just like such an  iconic cool thing that I'd have to say  that's close to my heart Russell you  know I adore you I adore talking with  you a little tease some point we're  gonna have a long-form interview you and  I we talked a lot about your career  that's gonna be on this weekend Marvel  but here I just say thanks for coming up  thank you giving this to me thank you  Robert for giving me this helmet a  really appreciate  you guys I mean I I wouldn't do this  without you so I'm big fans of yours  honestly and thanks for having me
 

